<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements for Glide Viewer.app (tools/make-viewer-app.sh). Deliberately
  empty, like glide-host.entitlements:
  - Video decoding (VideoToolbox), display (AVSampleBufferDisplayLayer) and audio playback: no
    entitlement. The viewer plays the PC's audio; it never records, so no audio-input.
  - Capturing system shortcuts while a session has focus (a CGEventTap at the session level):
    gated by Accessibility (TCC), not an entitlement. Without it the viewer falls back to a local
    event monitor.
  - Outgoing TCP to the PC and HTTPS to Glide Cloud: not sandboxed, so no network entitlement;
    macOS 15+ asks for Local Network access using NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription.
  - No JIT, unsigned memory, DYLD_* variables, library-validation exception or Apple Events.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
